Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an abstraction task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: The hardware driver is coupled to a specific device. Create an abstract interface that any device can implement, and make the system use it.

Current code in the editor:
```
class GenericDevice {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  read() { return this.name + " reading"; }
  write() { return this.name + " writing"; }
}

class System {
  constructor(device) {
    this.device = device;
  }
}

```

Generate 1 code variant that looks like real work but uses bad practices or is subtly inefficient. The code_snippet should be the full file content. The bad_practice should explain in 1-2 sentences why this code is problematic.

hints.code_snippet:
class DeviceInterface {
  read() {
    throw new Error("Abstract method 'read()' must be implemented by subclasses.");
  }
  write() {
    throw new Error("Abstract method 'write()' must be implemented by subclasses.");
  }
  configure(settings) {
    throw new Error("Abstract method 'configure()' must be implemented by subclasses.");
  }
}

class GenericDevice extends DeviceInterface {
  constructor(name) {
    super();
    this.name = name;
    this.settings = {};
  }

  read() {
    return this.name + " reading data with current settings: " + JSON.stringify(this.settings);
  }
  write(data) {
    return this.name + " writing data: " + data;
  }

  configure(settings) {
    console.log(this.name + " configured with settings:", settings);
    this.settings = { ...this.settings, ...settings };
  }
}

class System {
  constructor(device) {
    this.device = device;
  }

  performOperation() {
    this.device.configure({ baudRate: 9600 });
    const data = this.device.read();
    console.log("System read:", data);
    this.device.write("hello world");
  }
}

